#. DNS settings: description under the Fast DNS on connect toggle. Explains that it answers DNS over the local network while the tunnel's DNS starts, which can reveal lookups to the local network and can return answers that don't match the exit location (DNS answers depend on where the lookup comes from, so host-network answers can point to servers meant for the user's real location instead of the exit).
msgctxt "fast_dns_on_connect_description"
msgid "Answers DNS over the local network while the tunnel's DNS starts. This can reveal your lookups to the local network and return answers that don't match your exit location. When off, DNS only resolves through the tunnel."
msgstr "トンネルのDNSが起動するまで、ローカルネットワーク経由でDNSに応答します。問い合わせ内容がローカルネットワークに知られたり、出口の場所に合わない応答が返されたりする可能性があります。オフの場合、DNSはトンネル経由でのみ解決されます。"

